An electron is travelling in a straight line through a vacuum with a constant speed of $1.5 \times 10^{7}$ m s$^{-1}$. The electron enters a uniform electric field at point A, as shown in Fig. 5.1.

{{figure:figure_5_1.png}}

The electron continues to move in the same direction until it is brought to rest by the electric field at point B. Distance AB is 2.0 cm.
